"Internal Error ()\nciteturn8view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://petsymposium.org/popets/2026/popets-2026-0044.php\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://petsymposium.org/popets/2026/popets-2026-0044.php is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2404.16109] zkLLM: Zero Knowledge Proofs for Large Language Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16109)\nciteturn8view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16109\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 24 Apr 2024]\nL9: # Title:zkLLM: Zero Knowledge Proofs for Large Language Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Haochen Sun】, 【6†Jason Li】, 【7†Hongyang Zhang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled zkLLM: Zero Knowledge Proofs for Large Language Models, by Haochen Sun and Jason Li and Hongyang Zhang\nL14: \nL15: 【8†View PDF】 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:The recent surge in artificial intelligence (AI), characterized by the prominence of large language models (LLMs), has ushered in fundamental transformations across the globe. However, alongside these advancements, concerns surrounding the legitimacy of LLMs have grown, posing legal challenges to their extensive applications. Compounding these concerns, the parameters of LLMs are often treated as intellectual property, restricting direct investigations.\nL17: > In this study, we address a fundamental challenge within the realm of AI legislation: the need to establish the authenticity of outputs generated by LLMs. To tackle this issue, we present zkLLM, which stands as the inaugural specialized zero-knowledge proof tailored for LLMs to the best of our knowledge.\nL18: Addressing the persistent challenge of non-arithmetic operations in deep learning, we introduce tlookup, a parallelized lookup argument designed for non-arithmetic tensor operations in deep learning, offering a solution with no asymptotic overhead. Furthermore, leveraging the foundation of tlookup, we introduce zkAttn, a specialized zero-knowledge proof crafted for the attention mechanism, carefully balancing considerations of running time, memory usage, and accuracy.\nL19: > Empowered by our fully parallelized CUDA implementation, zkLLM emerges as a significant stride towards achieving efficient zero-knowledge verifiable computations over LLMs. Remarkably, for LLMs boasting 13 billion parameters, our approach enables the generation of a correctness proof for the entire inference process in under 15 minutes. The resulting proof, compactly sized at less than 200 kB, is designed to uphold the privacy of the model parameters, ensuring no inadvertent information leakage.\nL20: Comments:  | Accepted to ACM CCS 2024, camera-ready version under preparation. This is the author's version of the work. It is posted here for your personal use. Not for redistribution\nL21: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Cryptography and Security (cs.CR)\nL22: Cite as:  | 【10†arXiv:2404.16109】 [cs.LG]\nL23:    | (or 【11†arXiv:2404.16109v1】 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL24:    | 【12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2404.16109†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Haochen Sun [【13†view email】]\nL28: [v1] Wed, 24 Apr 2024 18:04:50 UTC (1,236 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled zkLLM: Zero Knowledge Proofs for Large Language Models, by Haochen Sun and Jason Li and Hongyang Zhang\nL35: \nL36:   * 【8†View PDF】\nL37:   * 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL38:   * 【14†TeX Source】\nL39: \nL40: 【15†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL41: ### Cu